#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""SYRD-417: the generated project config and layout upgrade, against the launcher it came out of.

The three definitions that bring a generated project's config and layout
template up to what this release generates moved unchanged into
`scripts/generated_layout_upgrade.py`, and the launcher re-exports all three.
This pins what makes that safe:

- **No cycle, one set of objects**, whichever module is imported first; the
  module alone loads no other Switchyard module; the definition-time defaults
  (`runner=subprocess.run`, `dry_run=False`) are the baseline's; the
  annotation types are imported under TYPE_CHECKING only.
- **Seams (rule 24):** every name the three read -- each other, the layout
  payloads and template check, the board root, the session directories, the
  shared pane launcher, the no-follow read, the atomic writer, the owner step
  and the result type -- is read through the launcher as often as before, so a
  patch there reaches it: every case below records or stands in for them there.
- **Callers:** `launch_project` calls the public entry point by its launcher
  global, and `upgrade_phases.py` reads it through the launcher.
- **The behaviour is the baseline's:** hand-maintained layouts are left
  alone; known generated shapes are upgraded, unknown ones never overwritten;
  detached roles are not counted; the directorctl pin, pane launcher and
  session directory; a dry run; the no-follow refusal after any layout write;
  a failing owner step; every message and every file in the tree afterwards.
  `GOLDEN` below was produced by running the BASELINE launcher's own functions
  over the very cases embedded here (`gold417.py`), not typed; it is
  byte-identical whether generated under `env -i` or in a normal role pane.

Every case builds its own test-owned provision tree; the no-follow read and
the atomic writer are the launcher's own, run inside it; the host's board root,
account lookups and session paths stand in; the owner step is a recorder and
the runner refuses. Spawns, every exec, signals, account and group lookups and
socket connections are refused for each case.
"""

